.TH SDL_GetAudioDeviceName 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetAudioDeviceName \- Get the human-readable name of a specific audio device.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_audio.h>
.PP
.BI "const char * SDL_GetAudioDeviceName(SDL_AudioDeviceID devid);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION

.BR WARNING :
this function will work with
.BR SDL_AUDIO_DEVICE_DEFAULT_PLAYBACK
and
.BR SDL_AUDIO_DEVICE_DEFAULT_RECORDING ,
returning the current default physical devices\(aq names\[char46] However, as the default device may change at any time, it is likely better to show a generic name to the user, like \(dqSystem default audio device\(dq or perhaps \(dqdefault [currently %s]\(dq\[char46] Do not store this name to disk to reidentify the device in a later run of the program, as the default might change in general, and the string will be the name of a specific device and not the abstract system default\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I devid
the instance ID of the device to query\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the name of the audio device, or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetAudioPlaybackDevices (3),
.BR SDL_GetAudioRecordingDevices (3)
